\date{2026-03-10T11:26:28Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}
\p{Let #{f : \Z \to \Z} be defined by #{f(x) = x+1}. Is #{f} invertible?

\ul{
  \li{Check: is it one-to-one? Yes; for any #{x, y \in \Z}, if #{x+1 = y+1} then #{x = y}.}
  \li{Onto? Yes, for any #{y \in \Z}, #{y-1 \in \Z} and #{f(y-1) = y}.}
}

Hence #{f} is invertible, and in fact, #{f^{-1}(x) = x-1}.}


